    "m_Description": "Neon Emission Shader Graph for NEON SERPENT.\n\nFeatures:\n- Base color with HDR emission\n- Fresnel rim glow for neon edge effect\n- Pulse animation support via Time node\n- Vertex color support for gradient effects\n\nTo use: Import this file into Unity's Shader Graph editor (URP).\nThe graph structure is described below for manual recreation.\n\nGraph Structure:\n1. Property: _BaseColor (Color, default Cyan)\n2. Property: _EmissionColor (Color, default White)\n3. Property: _EmissionIntensity (Float, default 2.0)\n4. Property: _FresnelPower (Float, default 2.0)\n5. Property: _PulseSpeed (Float, default 1.0)\n6. Property: _PulseAmount (Float, default 0.2)\n\nNodes:\n- Fresnel Effect (Power: _FresnelPower)\n- Time (Time)\n- Multiply (Time * _PulseSpeed)\n- Sine (sin(Multiply result))\n- Multiply (Sine * _PulseAmount)\n- Add (1.0 + Pulse Multiply)\n- Multiply (Fresnel * Add result)\n- Sample Texture 2D (Base Map)\n- Multiply (Sample * _BaseColor)\n- Vertex Color\n- Multiply (Base * Vertex Color)\n- Multiply (Fresnel result * _EmissionColor)\n- Multiply (Emission * _EmissionIntensity)\n- Add (Base result + Emission result)\n\nOutputs:\n- Base Color -> Fragment Base Color\n- Emission -> Fragment Emission\n- Alpha -> Fragment Alpha\n\nNote: This is a placeholder file. Unity Shader Graph files are binary\nand must be created within the Unity Editor. Use this as a reference\nto recreate the graph manually.\n"
}
